# What a Relay serves on its domain and on every Key Address under it (ADR 0020): iroh's paths go to
# tooob-relay (iroh-relay.toml), and everything else is the Bootstrap Bundle: its files, and its shell
# (index.html) at every other path, which is a page of a Site's (ADR 0023), except to a page's
# address saved outside the page ("Save link as"), which gets an explanation instead (#99).
# No Cookie goes on: a Relay needs none, and a Site that fills the Relay's domain with cookies would
# otherwise have iroh-relay refuse every other Host's Visitors (ADR 0021).
request_header -Cookie
@iroh path /relay /ping /generate_204 /healthz
handle @iroh {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3340
}
# Whether this Relay is open or carries only its Enrolled Keys' traffic (ADR 0030): tooob-relay's
# answer, not a Bundle file, so the Bundle's version.json stays as its Release made it.
handle /__tooob/relay.json {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3341
}
# A page's address saved outside the page ("Save link as", told apart by its Fetch Metadata) never
# reaches the Host: only the page can fetch a Site's files. The shell would save as an empty page,
# so the saved file says so instead (#99). Chromium (Chrome, Brave) asks with Dest empty and Mode
# navigate; Firefox with Dest empty and Mode no-cors, the Fetch spec's own for a download. A page
# visit is Dest document: the shell. Safari sends no Fetch Metadata here, so it gets the shell.
@saved {
	not path /__tooob/* /tooob-sw.js
	header Sec-Fetch-Dest empty
	header_regexp Sec-Fetch-Mode ^(navigate|no-cors)$
}
handle @saved {
	header Cache-Control "no-store"
	# A folder's address has no file name, and no Download link.
	@folder path */
	respond @folder <<TXT
		This isn't {http.request.uri.path}. tooob can only fetch it from inside the page:
		open the link in your browser.
		TXT 200
	respond <<TXT
		This isn't {http.request.uri.path.file}. tooob can only fetch it from inside the page:
		open the link in your browser and use ⬇ Download next to the file.
		TXT 200
}
handle {
	root * /srv
	# The Bundle's files change with every upgrade and the pages are small: make browsers recheck
	# them each time (cheap 304s), so an upgrade reaches phones at once, not after a cache expiry.
	header Cache-Control "no-cache"
	# Every Key Address shares one site without the Public Suffix List: ask for a process of its
	# own anyway (ADR 0021). No Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy, which breaks Sites that load from
	# elsewhere, and COOP's same-origin would break login popups.
	header Origin-Agent-Cluster "?1"
	header Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy "same-origin-allow-popups"
	# A page's address saved outside the page is the explanation above: never answer one with the
	# other from a cache.
	header Vary "Sec-Fetch-Dest, Sec-Fetch-Mode"
	# A page's own address, opened before the service worker is installed (a first visit), is the
	# shell, which opens that page. A missing Bundle file stays a 404.
	@page {
		not path /__tooob/* /tooob-sw.js
		not file
	}
	rewrite @page /index.html
	# The brotli and gzip copies the image build made beside each file (#113): the WASM is 3.1 MB
	# as is, 795 KB as brotli. Nothing is compressed on the fly, so a Relay spends no CPU on it.
	# file_server adds Accept-Encoding to the Vary above.
	file_server {
		precompressed br gzip
	}
}
